(11.5 LOGGING WITH ECK, ELASTICSEARCH, KIBANA, AND FLUENTD) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The platform installs the ECK operator and then applies local Elasticsearch/Kibana/Fluentd) Tj
T*
(resources. Elasticsearch runs version 8.16.1 as a single node with a 5 Gi persistent volume and) Tj
T*
(JVM heap set to 512 Mi. Kibana runs version 8.16.1 and connects to that Elasticsearch cluster.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Fluentd runs as a DaemonSet on the AKS user node pool. It tails/var/log/containers/*.log, parses) Tj
T*
(CRI log format, enriches records with Kubernetes metadata, attempts to parse the Spring JSON log) Tj
T*
(message, and ships records to Elasticsearch using logstash-style indices with prefixasbdemo. It) Tj
T*
(reads the Elasticsearch password from the ECK-generatedelasticsearch-es-elastic-usersecret.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(12. CI/CD AUTOMATION) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(12.1 GITHUB ACTIONS APPLICATION PIPELINE) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Theapp-ciworkflow runs on pull requests and pushes tomainthat touch application files. It) Tj
T*
(computes a seven-character image tag from the Git SHA, builds both Docker images with Docker) Tj
T*
(Buildx, scans them with Trivy for HIGH and CRITICAL vulnerabilities, logs in to Azure using OIDC) Tj
T*
(on pushes, pushes images to ACR, and then updates the GitOps Kustomize image tags.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The GitOps bump job installs Kustomize 5.4.3, runskustomize edit set imagefor both services,) Tj
T*
(commitsgitops/workloads/envs/dev/kustomization.yaml, and pushes back to the repository. This) Tj
T*
(commit is the handoff point from CI to ArgoCD.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(12.2 GITHUB ACTIONS TERRAFORM PIPELINE) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The Terraform workflow runs on infrastructure changes. It performsterraform fmt -check,) Tj
T*
(initializes without backend for validation, validates the stack, runs a full plan through HCP) Tj
T*
(Terraform, and posts the plan outcome to a pull request or commit. Applies run only on pushes) Tj
T*
(tomainand are protected by theazure-devGitHub environment.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(12.3 AZURE DEVOPS PIPELINE MIRRORS) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The repository also includes Azure DevOps equivalents. The app pipeline builds, scans, pushes to) Tj
T*
(ACR, fetches a GitHub PAT from Key Vault, and commits the GitOps image bump. The Terraform) Tj
T*
(pipeline installs Terraform, fetches the HCP Terraform token from Key Vault, validates, plans,) Tj
T*
(and applies from an environment-gated deployment job. These files provide an alternate CI/CD) Tj
T*
(implementation while preserving the same delivery model.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(13. SECURITY AND IDENTITY MODEL) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The strongest security design in the project is the use of short-lived federated identities) Tj
T*
(rather than static secrets for core automation and application access.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- HCP Terraform can authenticate to Azure through OIDC federation, as described in the runbook.) Tj
T*
(- GitHub Actions uses Azure OIDC login for ACR push operations.) Tj
T*
(- AKS has OIDC issuer and workload identity enabled.) Tj
T*
(- Each application pod uses a dedicated Kubernetes service account annotated with the correct) Tj
ET
