T*
(15. CURRENT IMPLEMENTATION NOTES AND RECOMMENDED NEXT STEPS) Tj
T*
(Validation performed while generating this document:the workload, platform apps, and elastic) Tj
T*
(kustomizations all rendered successfully withkubectl kustomize.) Tj
T*
(- No Java unit or integration tests are currently present underapp/**/src/test. Adding) Tj
T*
(controller tests, serialization tests, and Service Bus client boundary tests would improve) Tj
T*
(confidence.) Tj
T*
(- The README mentions cert-manager and TLS, and cert-manager is installed, but the current) Tj
T*
(workload manifests only define an HTTP listener and no ClusterIssuer, Certificate, or HTTPS) Tj
T*
(Gateway listener.) Tj
T*
(- The Gateway and platform services are mostly ClusterIP, which is appropriate for a private dev) Tj
T*
(setup. External access requires additional load balancer or ingress exposure work.) Tj
T*
(- Service Bus local auth and public network access are enabled in Terraform. For production,) Tj
T*
(consider disabling local auth after confirming Azure AD-only access, and restrict network access) Tj
T*
(through private endpoints or firewall rules.) Tj
T*
(- Kubernetes ServiceAccount annotations currently contain concrete client IDs, and workload) Tj
T*
(manifests contain concrete Service Bus FQDN and ACR names. A stronger multi-environment design) Tj
T*
(would template these through overlays or generated configuration.) Tj
T*
(- Grafana uses the demo passwordadminand has no persistence. For longer-lived environments, move) Tj
T*
(credentials to a secret manager and enable persistent storage.) Tj
T*
(- The Grafana dashboard referencesservicebus_queue_active_messages. That metric requires an) Tj
T*
(exporter or Azure Monitor integration to be present; the current codebase does not define a) Tj
T*
(Service Bus exporter.) Tj
T*
(- The Terraform Key Vault is provisioned and used by Azure DevOps pipeline documentation, but) Tj
T*
(the Kubernetes workloads are not yet wired to Key Vault CSI in the current manifests.) Tj
T*
